# Narrator: the Grey Goose, a burned-out roadhouse on the Old Svalich Road (The Lantern in the Roadhouse,
# docs/story/side_quests.md; docs/voice/narrator.md). Every line here is unvoiced for now.

~ enter:svalich_roadhouse
| A roadhouse by the road, burned to its walls a long time ago. A painted goose still hangs from the sign-iron, grey with soot.
| [night] A burned-out roadhouse, and high in its front, where an upstairs window used to be, a lantern burning steadily in the empty air.
| [flag.roadhouse_cellar_beaten] The Grey Goose is only a ruin now, and the road goes past it without looking.
cooldown 30

~ examine:roadhouse_hearth
| The hearth stands on its own among the weeds like a tombstone. Its stone is cracked across, and under the crack, a hollow.

~ examine:roadhouse_sign
| THE GREY GOOSE, says the sign, over a painted goose with a hat on. Under it, in fresher paint, somebody has added: GO ON.
